This is the classic case of three correct-looking declarations that do nothing. A flex item&#x27;s min-width starts at auto, and for a flex item auto means &#x27;never smaller than the content&#x27;s minimum size&#x27;. So even with flex:1 the item refuses to shrink below its content, the long text pushes the container open, and overflow: hidden never gets a chance to clip. Setting min-width: 0 removes that floor and the ellipsis finally appears. Review shortcut: whenever text-overflow: ellipsis appears on a flex item, look for min-width: 0 nearby. flex-wrap: wrap would move the whole item to a new line, which changes the design intent rather than truncating the text.
这是「三个属性都写对了却不生效」的经典案例。flex 子项的 min-width 初始值是 auto，而 auto 对 flex 子项的含义是「不小于内容的最小尺寸」。所以哪怕写了 flex:1，子项也不会收缩到内容宽度以下，长文本把容器顶开，overflow: hidden 根本没机会生效。设 min-width: 0 解除这个下限，省略号才会出现。审查口诀：flex 子项上出现 text-overflow: ellipsis，就往下找 min-width: 0。flex-wrap: wrap 会让整个子项换行，改变的是设计意图，不是截断文本。
