TypeScript code review
This never assignment checks that every action was handled. Which missing implementation should the reviewer request?
这里的 never 赋值用于检查是否处理了所有动作。审查者应要求补上哪个实现？
never への代入で全アクションの処理漏れを検査している。何を追加すべきか。
type Action = { type: &quot;save&quot; } | { type: &quot;delete&quot; };
function handle(action: Action): string {
  switch (action.type) {
    case &quot;save&quot;: return &quot;saved&quot;;
    default: {
      const unhandled: never = action;
      return unhandled;
    }
  }
}
A. Add case &quot;delete&quot; with its own return path, leaving the never check.
B. Delete the never check and silently treat delete as save.
C. Rename unhandled to handled; names control exhaustive checking.
D. Replace never with any because any proves every case is handled.
Reference answer: A
After save returns, delete still reaches default, so action is not never. Add the missing delete branch. Keeping the never check makes a future unhandled action a type error instead of a silent fall-through.
save 返回后，delete 仍会进入 default，因此 action 还不是 never。应补上 delete 分支。保留 never 检查，可以让未来新增但未处理的动作触发类型错误，而非悄悄漏掉。
save の処理後も delete が default に到達するので action は never ではない。delete 分岐を追加する。never の検査を残せば、将来の追加時も処理漏れを型エラーとして検出できる。
